---TechnologyWatchListAlertThreshold contains the thresholds for alerting.
---@class gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.TechnologyWatchListAlertThreshold
---@field riskRatingMinimum? gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.TechnologyWatchListAlertThresholdRiskRatingMinimumEnum|string Optional. The minimum risk rating for the alert.
---@field cvssScoreMinimum? number Optional. The minimum CVSS score for the alert. Evaluates to CVSS v3 when available with a fallback to v2 and v4. Ex: 7.0. Valid range is [0.0, 10.0].
---@field epssScoreMinimum? number Optional. The minimum epss score for the alert. Ex: 0.8. Valid range is [0.0, 1.0].
---@field exploitationStates? gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.TechnologyWatchListAlertThresholdExploitationStatesItemEnumList Optional. The exploitation states of the alert.
---@field priorityMinimum? gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.TechnologyWatchListAlertThresholdPriorityMinimumEnum|string Optional. The minimum priority for the alert.

---@alias gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.TechnologyWatchListAlertThresholdExploitationStatesItemEnum "EXPLOITATION_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"EXPLOITATION_STATE_NO_KNOWN"|"EXPLOITATION_STATE_REPORTED"|"EXPLOITATION_STATE_SUSPECTED"|"EXPLOITATION_STATE_CONFIRMED"|"EXPLOITATION_STATE_WIDESPREAD"

---@alias gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.TechnologyWatchListAlertThresholdExploitationStatesItemEnumList (gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.TechnologyWatchListAlertThresholdExploitationStatesItemEnum|string)[]

---@alias gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.TechnologyWatchListAlertThresholdPriorityMinimumEnum "PRIORITY_UNSPECIFIED"|"P0"|"P1"|"P2"|"P3"|"P4"

---@alias gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.TechnologyWatchListAlertThresholdRiskRatingMinimumEnum "RISK_RATING_UNSPECIFIED"|"LOW"|"MEDIUM"|"HIGH"|"CRITICAL"|"UNRATED"

---TechnologyWatchListConfig is the configuration for the technology watchlist.
---@class gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.TechnologyWatchListConfig
---@field technologies? gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.StringList Optional. List of technologies to watch, one per entry, in the form ` [version]`, using the vendor and product names from the Google Threat Intelligence products and fixes section. example: `microsoft outlook` `apache http_server 2.4.54` CPE strings such as `cpe:2.3:a:microsoft:outlook:*:*:*:*:*:*:*:*` are only parsed through the Google Threat Intelligence interface and are not available through the API. Send the vendor and product pair instead.
---@field alertThreshold? gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.TechnologyWatchListAlertThreshold Optional. Alert thresholds to effectively reduce noise.

