---Response message for UpsertConfiguration.
---@class gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.UpsertConfigurationResponse
---@field configuration? string Output only. Created configuration ID with server assigned id.

---@class gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.UpsertProjectsConfigurationsRequest
---@field displayName? string Output only. Human readable name for the configuration.
---@field detail? gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.ConfigurationDetail Required. Domain specific details for the configuration.
---@field etag? string If included when updating a configuration, this should be set to the current etag of the configuration. If the etags do not match, the update will be rejected and an ABORTED error will be returned.
---@field state? gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.ConfigurationStateEnum|string Optional. State of the configuration.
---@field description? string Optional. A description of the configuration.
---@field provider? string Required. Name of the service that provides the configuration.
---@field version? string Optional. A user-manipulatable version. Does not adhere to a specific format
---@field audit? gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.Audit Output only. Audit information for the configuration.
---@field name? string Identifier. Server generated name for the configuration. format is projects/{project}/configurations/{configuration}
---@field publishTime? string Optional. Time that the configuration should be considered to have been published. This is an advanced feature used when onboarding and bulk loading data from other systems. Do not set this field without consulting with the API team.
---@field parent string Required. Parent of the configuration.

---Contains details about a vulnerability match.
---@class gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.VulnerabilityMatch
---@field collectionId? string Required. The collection ID of the vulnerability. Ex: "vulnerability--cve-2025-9876".
---@field riskRating? gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.VulnerabilityMatchRiskRatingEnum Required. The risk rating of the vulnerability.
---@field description? string Required. A description of the vulnerability.
---@field matchedTechnologies? gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.StringList Optional. The entries from the configured watchlist that triggered the match, exactly as written in `TechnologyWatchListConfig.technologies`. Ex: `apache http_server 2.4.54`.
---@field priority? gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.VulnerabilityMatchPriorityEnum Optional. The priority level of the vulnerability data. Ex: "P1".
---@field exploitationConsequences? gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.VulnerabilityMatchExploitationConsequencesItemEnumList Optional. List of exploitation consequences for the vulnerability.
---@field cvss3Score? number Required. The CVSS score of the vulnerability. Evaluates to CVSS v3 when available with a fallback to v2 and v4. Example: 6.4.
---@field cveId? string Required. The CVE ID of the vulnerability. Ex: "CVE-2025-9876". See https://www.cve.org/ for more information.
---@field technologies? gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.StringList Required. All technologies affected by the vulnerability, using the vendor and product names of its affected products, optionally followed by a version. Ex: `Apache Struts 2.2.3`.
---@field publicExploits? gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.PublicExploitList Optional. List of public exploits.
---@field disclosureTime? string Optional. The disclosure time of the vulnerability.
---@field exploitationState? gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.VulnerabilityMatchExploitationStateEnum Required. The exploitation state of the vulnerability.
---@field epssScore? number Optional. The EPSS score, representing the probability of exploitation. Example: 0.87.
---@field productFixes? gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.ProductFixList Optional. List of product fixes for the vulnerability.
---@field publiclyAvailableExploit? boolean Output only. Whether a publicly available exploit exists.
---@field associations? gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.AssociationList Optional. Associated threat actors, malware, etc. This is embedded as a snapshot because the details of the association at the time of the vulnerability match are important for context and reporting.
---@field exploitationVectors? gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.VulnerabilityMatchExploitationVectorsItemEnumList Optional. List of exploitation vectors for the vulnerability.

---@alias gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.VulnerabilityMatchExploitationConsequencesItemEnum "EXPLOITATION_CONSEQUENCE_UNSPECIFIED"|"CODE_EXECUTION"|"COMMAND_EXECUTION"|"DATA_LOSS"|"DATA_MANIPULATION"|"DENIAL_OF_SERVICE"|"INFORMATION_DISCLOSURE"|"UNAUTHORIZED_ACCESS"|"PRIVILEGE_ESCALATION"|"SANDBOX_ESCAPE"|"SECURITY_BYPASS"|"CONTAINER_ESCAPE"|"SPOOFING"

---@alias gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.VulnerabilityMatchExploitationConsequencesItemEnumList gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.VulnerabilityMatchExploitationConsequencesItemEnum[]

---@alias gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.VulnerabilityMatchExploitationStateEnum "EXPLOITATION_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"EXPLOITATION_STATE_NO_KNOWN"|"EXPLOITATION_STATE_REPORTED"|"EXPLOITATION_STATE_SUSPECTED"|"EXPLOITATION_STATE_CONFIRMED"|"EXPLOITATION_STATE_WIDESPREAD"

---@alias gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.VulnerabilityMatchExploitationVectorsItemEnum "EXPLOITATION_VECTOR_UNSPECIFIED"|"ADMINISTRATIVE_INTERFACE"|"BLUETOOTH_ACCESS"|"BROWSER"|"COMPROMISED_COMMUNICATION_CHANNEL"|"EMAIL"|"EXPOSED_WEB_APPLICATION"|"LOCAL_NETWORK_ACCESS"|"MALICIOUS_APPLICATION"|"MALICIOUS_FILE"|"MALICIOUS_SERVER"|"OPEN_PORT"|"PHYSICAL_ACCESS"|"SHORT_RANGE_RADIO"|"UNSPECIFIED_LOCAL_VECTOR"|"UNSPECIFIED_REMOTE_VECTOR"|"VPN_ACCESS"|"WIFI_ACCESS"

---@alias gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.VulnerabilityMatchExploitationVectorsItemEnumList gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.VulnerabilityMatchExploitationVectorsItemEnum[]

---@alias gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.VulnerabilityMatchPriorityEnum "PRIORITY_UNSPECIFIED"|"P0"|"P1"|"P2"|"P3"|"P4"

---@alias gcp.threatintelligence_v1beta.VulnerabilityMatchRiskRatingEnum "RISK_RATING_UNSPECIFIED"|"LOW"|"MEDIUM"|"HIGH"|"CRITICAL"|"UNRATED"

